<title>CANADA: Canada government cash balances fall in week.</title>
<headline>Canada government cash balances fall in week.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The government of Canada's cash balances fall in the week that ended January 29, the Bank of Canada said on Friday.</p>
<p>				     Wk to Jan 29 Chg on wk Chg on yr</p>
<p>Notes in circulation		  26.75   +0.104    +0.638</p>
<p>Government cash balances	     2.63   -1.448    -0.398</p>
<p>Govt securities outstanding	461.18   -0.711    +5.456</p>
<p>Treasury bills			 131.20   -0.700   -26.400</p>
<p>Canada savings bonds		  33.37   -0.011    +2.116</p>
<p>All figures in billions of dollars.  </p>
<p>   Chartered bank assets			 Dec	   Nov</p>
<p>   Net foreign currency			-13.81	-12.67</p>
<p>   Canadian dollar			     681.94	678.44</p>
<p>   Total Canadian liquid assets	    108.04	109.17</p>
<p>					   Dec 96     Nov 96     Dec 95</p>
<p>M1					  69.74	67.19	61.47</p>
<p>M2					 398.32     397.35     388.64</p>
<p>M3					 500.53     498.68     474.12</p>
<p>Note - Figures are unadjusted, in billions of dollars.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau (613) 235-6745))</p>
